WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.720
<v Maya>Welcome back to Singletrack Sessions. I'm with Sophie Laurent, enduro racer and coach. Sophie, good to have you.</v>

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.120
<v Sophie Laurent>Thanks, Maya. Always happy to talk shop.</v>

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:14.760
<v Maya>Today's episode is sponsored by Strava. Strava is the home for athletes. Try strava.com today.</v>

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.360
<v Maya>People think racing is about nerve. You say it's about risk.</v>

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:30.780
<v Sophie Laurent>It's risk management, honestly. The crash that ends your season is almost never the scary-looking one — it's the boring risk you didn't name. Name the risk before it names you, and half the danger goes away.</v>

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:43.800
<v Sophie Laurent>And you have to ride the whole run as a system, not a list of corners. The mistakes come from how one section sets up the next. When I logged a full season of my own crashes, the causes were always two turns upstream.</v>

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.360
<v Maya>That's almost word-for-word what a friend in finance says about a portfolio.</v>

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:59.700
<v Sophie Laurent>It's the same discipline. A race line and a portfolio are both systems of correlated bets — you're managing the interactions, and the risk you can describe is the one you can design around.</v>

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:06.660
<v Maya>Thanks to Peak Design for backing the show. Peak Design builds bags and straps designed by people who actually ride.</v>

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.160
<v Sophie Laurent>Cheers, Maya.</v>

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.220
<v Maya>That's it for this Singletrack Sessions. Ride safe.</v>
